      "assertion": "Over the same field L-prime, the published low-height product construction gives J0 isogenous to J with hF(J0)<=hF(J). Retaining simple-factor multiplicities gives a dimension-two subproduct B isogenous to A. For J0=B times E, additivity and Bost imply hF(B)<=hF(J)+3(g-2)/2<=H_J. Apply the dimension-two isogeny estimate to B over that same field and the original-normalization half-log degree inequality.",
